/-!
# The inverse-image ideal of an affine morphism of algebraic spaces

Let `f : Y ⟶ X` be a representable morphism of algebraic spaces over a scheme `S` contained in
a big fppf site `B` and let `I ⊆ 𝒪_X` be a sheaf of ideals on the small étale site of `X`.  The
inverse image `f⁻¹I` is a sheaf of ideals of `f⁻¹𝒪_X`, and it acts on the `𝒪_Y`-modules through
the structure map `f♯ : f⁻¹𝒪_X ⟶ 𝒪_Y` of Stacks 03G8.  Its image in `𝒪_Y` under that action —
the sheaf of ideals generated by the pulled-back sections of `I` — is built here, together with
the transport of covering sieves from the small étale site of `X` to that of `Y` which comparing
it with `I` needs.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsPullbackIdealUpperBound` is the property of a sheaf of ideals of
  `𝒪_Y` of containing every pulled-back section `f♯(a)` of `I` over a base-changed chart.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pullbackIdealSubsheaf` is the smallest such sheaf of ideals, that is,
  the image of `f⁻¹I` in `𝒪_Y`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.coverPreserving_smallBaseChange`: small-chart base change along a
  representable morphism of algebraic spaces is cover preserving, so a covering sieve of a chart
  `Q` of `X` has a covering sieve of `Q ×_X Y` as its image.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.etalePrecoverage_smallBaseChange_ofArrows`: the family of base-changed
  charts of an étale covering family of charts of `X` is an étale covering family of schemes.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartIdealPullbackHom_mem_pullbackIdealSubsheaf` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pullbackIdealSubsheaf_le`: the characterizing properties of the
  inverse-image ideal, namely that it contains the pulled-back sections of `I` and is contained
  in every sheaf of ideals that does.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_idealSmul_pullback_of_mem_pushforward`: one inclusion of
  Stacks 0GF8 as an inclusion of subsheaves of `f_*F`, namely

  `I · f_*F ⊆ f_*((f⁻¹I) · F)`,

  read on sections over every étale chart of `X`.  No affineness and no quasi-coherence are
  needed for it; representability of `f` is all that enters.
* `Stacks.Sites.mem_idealSmul_iff` and `Stacks.Sites.mem_idealSmul_of_mem`: a section lies in
  the product of a sheaf of ideals with a submodule exactly when it lies in the objectwise
  product locally.

## Implementation notes

The inverse-image ideal is built as an infimum rather than as the closure of an objectwise
submodule: a section of `𝒪_Y` lies in it exactly when it lies locally in the ideal generated by
the pulled-back sections, and the infimum of submodules whose membership is local is computed
objectwise, which is what makes `SheafOfModules.Submodule.mem_sInf_obj` available.  The two
characterizing properties are all that is used of it downstream.

Cover preservation of small-chart base change is new here.  The continuity of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isContinuous_smallBaseChange` is proved through the comparison with the
spaces-étale site and the restriction of sheaves along it, and so says nothing about the image
of an individual covering sieve; and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smallBaseChange_isCoverDense_of_isClosedImmersion` is about closed
immersions.  The proof
here is the direct one: a covering family of charts of `X` is, by definition, an étale covering
family of the underlying schemes, the underlying scheme of a base-changed chart is the fibre
product of schemes by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.representablePullbackMap_isPullback_scheme`, and the étale precoverage
of schemes is stable under base change.

*The inclusion proved here.*  A section of `I · f_*F` over a chart `Q` of `X` lies, on a covering
sieve of `Q`, in the objectwise product `I(Q') · (f_*F)(Q')`.  The sections of `f_*F` over `Q'`
are the sections of `F` over `Q' ×_X Y` with the action restricted along `f♯`, so that objectwise
product is already an objectwise product for the inverse-image ideal over `Q' ×_X Y`; cover
preservation turns the covering sieve of `Q` into a covering sieve of `Q ×_X Y`, which is what
the local description of the product on `Y` consumes.  The opposite inclusion rests on a further
ingredient: the product on `Y` computed objectwise over an affine chart, which is a descent
statement for the inverse-image ideal.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GF8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GF8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03G2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03G2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03G8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03G8)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Opposite

universe w v₁ u₁ m u

namespace Stacks.Sites


variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})] {O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{u}}
  {M : SheafOfModules.{w} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)}

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})] in
/-- **Local membership characterizes the product of a sheaf of ideals with a submodule.**  A
section of a sheaf of modules lies in `I · N` exactly when it restricts into the objectwise
product along every arrow of some covering sieve. -/
theorem mem_idealSmul_iff {I : IdealSubsheaf O} {N : M.Submodule} {Z : Cᵒᵖ}
    {x : M.val.obj Z} :
    x ∈ (idealSmul I N).obj Z ↔
      ∃ T : Sieve Z.unop, T ∈ J Z.unop ∧
        ∀ ⦃W : C⦄ (g : W ⟶ Z.unop), T g →
          M.val.map g.op x ∈ (presheafIdealSmul I N.toSubmodule).obj (op W) :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.mem_sheafifySubmodule_iff

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})] in
/-- A section restricting into the objectwise product along every arrow of a covering sieve lies
in `I · N`. -/
theorem mem_idealSmul_of_mem {I : IdealSubsheaf O} {N : M.Submodule} {Z : Cᵒᵖ}
    {x : M.val.obj Z} {T : Sieve Z.unop} (hT : T ∈ J Z.unop)
    (hx : ∀ ⦃W : C⦄ (g : W ⟶ Z.unop), T g →
      M.val.map g.op x ∈ (presheafIdealSmul I N.toSubmodule).obj (op W)) :
    x ∈ (idealSmul I N).obj Z :=
  mem_idealSmul_iff.2 ⟨T, hT, hx⟩

end Stacks.Sites

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

noncomputable section

attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isContinuous_smallBaseChange

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
variable {X Y : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS}

/-! ### Cover preservation of small-chart base change -/

/-- **The base change of an étale covering family of charts is an étale covering family of
schemes.**  The underlying scheme of the base change of a chart morphism is the fibre product of
schemes, by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.representablePullbackMap_isPullback_scheme`, and the étale
precoverage of schemes is stable under base change. -/
theorem etalePrecoverage_smallBaseChange_ofArrows (f : Y ⟶ X)
    (hf : yoneda.relativelyRepresentable f.hom) {Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} {ι : Type*}
    (Z : ι → SmallEtale B S hS X.1) (a : ∀ i, Z i ⟶ Q)
    (h : Presieve.ofArrows
        (fun i ↦ (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj (Z i)))
        (fun i ↦ (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map
          ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).map (a i))) ∈
      Scheme.etalePrecoverage
        ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj Q))) :
    Presieve.ofArrows
        (fun i ↦ (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS Y.1).obj
          ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj (Z i))))
        (fun i ↦ (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS Y.1).map
          ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).map (a i)))) ∈
      Scheme.etalePrecoverage
        ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS Y.1).obj
          ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q))) :=
  Precoverage.mem_coverings_of_isPullback _ h
    ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (hf.snd Q.1.hom)) _
    (fun i ↦ (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (hf.snd (Z i).1.hom))
    fun i ↦ representablePullbackMap_isPullback_scheme B S hS f hf (a i)

/-- **Small-chart base change along a representable morphism of algebraic spaces is cover
preserving.**  A covering sieve of a chart `Q` of `X` contains a covering family of charts, whose
base change is a covering family of charts of `Q ×_X Y` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.etalePrecoverage_smallBaseChange_ofArrows`, and that family is contained
in the image sieve.

This is what transports a covering sieve from the small étale site of `X` to the one of `Y`;
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isContinuous_smallBaseChange` does not, being proved through the
restriction of sheaves along the comparison with the spaces-étale site. -/
theorem coverPreserving_smallBaseChange (f : Y ⟶ X)
    (hf : yoneda.relativelyRepresentable f.hom) :
    CoverPreserving (SmallEtale.topology B S hS X.1) (SmallEtale.topology B S hS Y.1)
      (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf) := by
  have := preservesPullbacks_smallBaseChange B S hS f hf
  refine coverPreserving_of_generators _ (SmallEtale.precoverage B S hS X.1) _ ?_
  intro Q R hR
  obtain ⟨E, rfl, hE⟩ := hR
  have h1 : Presieve.ofArrows E.X E.f ∈ SmallEtale.precoverage B S hS X.1 Q := ⟨E, rfl, hE⟩
  rw [SmallEtale.precoverage_eq_comap, Precoverage.mem_comap_iff,
    BigFppfSite.etalePrecoverage_eq_comap, Precoverage.mem_comap_iff,
    Presieve.map_ofArrows, Presieve.map_ofArrows] at h1
  have h2 := etalePrecoverage_smallBaseChange_ofArrows B S hS f hf E.X E.f h1
  refine (SmallEtale.topology B S hS Y.1).superset_covering ?_
    (SmallEtale.ofArrows_mem_topology B S hS Y.1
      (fun i ↦ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj (E.X i))
      (fun i ↦ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).map (E.f i)) h2)
  rintro V v ⟨W, w, g, ⟨i⟩, rfl⟩
  exact ⟨E.X i, E.f i, w, ⟨E.X i, 𝟙 _, E.f i, ⟨i⟩, by simp⟩, rfl⟩

/-! ### The inverse-image ideal -/

variable (f : Y ⟶ X) (hf : yoneda.relativelyRepresentable f.hom)
  (I : (SheafOfModules.unit (smallEtaleRingSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2)).Submodule)

/-- A sheaf of ideals of `𝒪_Y` *bounds the inverse-image ideal* when, for every étale chart `Q`
of `X`, its sections over the base-changed chart `Q ×_X Y` contain the pullback `f♯(a)` of every
section `a` of `I` over `Q`.

These are the local sections which the source uses to describe `f⁻¹I` acting on `𝒪_Y`. -/
def IsPullbackIdealUpperBound
    (P : (SheafOfModules.unit (smallEtaleRingSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2)).Submodule) : Prop :=
  ∀ (Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1) (a : chartSectionsRing B S hS X Q),
    a ∈ chartSectionsIdeal B S hS X I Q →
      chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf Q a ∈
        P.obj (op ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q))

/-- **The inverse-image ideal `f⁻¹I · 𝒪_Y`**: the smallest sheaf of ideals of `𝒪_Y` containing
the pullback along `f♯` of every section of `I` over an étale chart of `X`.

This is the image in `𝒪_Y` of the sheaf of ideals `f⁻¹I` of `f⁻¹𝒪_X` under the structure map
`f♯` of Stacks 03G8, which is the ideal that acts on the `𝒪_Y`-modules in Stacks 0GF8. -/
def pullbackIdealSubsheaf :
    (SheafOfModules.unit (smallEtaleRingSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2)).Submodule :=
  sInf {P | IsPullbackIdealUpperBound B S hS f hf I P}

/-- The inverse-image ideal contains the pullback of every section of `I` over an étale chart. -/
theorem chartIdealPullbackHom_mem_pullbackIdealSubsheaf
    (Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1) {a : chartSectionsRing B S hS X Q}
    (ha : a ∈ chartSectionsIdeal B S hS X I Q) :
    chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf Q a ∈
      (pullbackIdealSubsheaf B S hS f hf I).obj
        (op ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q)) :=
  (_root_.SheafOfModules.Submodule.mem_sInf_obj _ _ _).2 fun _ hP => hP Q a ha

/-- The inverse-image ideal is the smallest sheaf of ideals containing the pullbacks of the
sections of `I`. -/
theorem pullbackIdealSubsheaf_le
    {P : (SheafOfModules.unit (smallEtaleRingSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2)).Submodule}
    (hP : IsPullbackIdealUpperBound B S hS f hf I P) :
    pullbackIdealSubsheaf B S hS f hf I ≤ P :=
  sInf_le hP

/-- The inverse-image ideal is a sheaf of ideals bounding itself, that is, it is a fixed point of
the description it is built from. -/
theorem isPullbackIdealUpperBound_pullbackIdealSubsheaf :
    IsPullbackIdealUpperBound B S hS f hf I (pullbackIdealSubsheaf B S hS f hf I) :=
  fun Q _ ha => chartIdealPullbackHom_mem_pullbackIdealSubsheaf B S hS f hf I Q ha

/-! ### One inclusion of Stacks 0GF8 -/

variable (F : SheafOfModules.{m} (smallEtaleRingSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2))

/-- **The objectwise product `I · f_*F` over a chart `Q` of `X` lands in the objectwise product
`(f⁻¹I) · F` over the base-changed chart `Q ×_X Y`.**

The sections of `f_*F` over `Q` are the sections of `F` over `Q ×_X Y` with the `𝒪_X(Q)`-action
restricted along `f♯`, so a product `a · s` with `a` a section of `I` over `Q` is the product
`f♯(a) · s`, and `f♯(a)` is a section of the inverse-image ideal. -/
theorem mem_presheafIdealSmul_pullback_of_mem_pushforward (Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    {z : F.val.obj (op ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q))}
    (hz : z ∈ (Stacks.Sites.presheafIdealSmul (O := structureSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2) I
      (⊤ : ((smallBaseChangeModulePushforward B S hS f hf).obj F).Submodule).toSubmodule).obj
        (op Q)) :
    z ∈ (Stacks.Sites.presheafIdealSmul (O := structureSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2)
      (pullbackIdealSubsheaf B S hS f hf I) (⊤ : F.Submodule).toSubmodule).obj
        (op ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q)) := by
  induction hz using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem w hw =>
    obtain ⟨a, ha, m, -, rfl⟩ := hw
    have htop : (m : F.val.obj (op ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q))) ∈
        (⊤ : F.Submodule).toSubmodule.obj (op ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q)) := by
      rw [Stacks.SheafOfModules.toSubmodule_top]; trivial
    exact Stacks.Sites.smul_mem_presheafIdealSmul _
      (chartIdealPullbackHom_mem_pullbackIdealSubsheaf B S hS f hf I Q ha) htop
  | zero => exact Submodule.zero_mem _
  | add _ _ _ _ h1 h2 => exact Submodule.add_mem _ h1 h2
  | smul r _ _ h1 =>
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ (chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf Q r) h1

/-- A section of `f_*F` over a chart `Q` of `X` lying in the objectwise product `I · f_*F` along
a covering sieve of `Q` lies in the product `(f⁻¹I) · F` over `Q ×_X Y`.

The image of the covering sieve under small-chart base change is a covering sieve of `Q ×_X Y`
by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.coverPreserving_smallBaseChange`, and restricting along an arrow of
it factors through the base change of an arrow of the given sieve. -/
theorem mem_idealSmul_pullback_of_forall (Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    {x : F.val.obj (op ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q))}
    {T : Sieve Q} (hT : T ∈ SmallEtale.topology B S hS X.1 Q)
    (hmem : ∀ ⦃Z : SmallEtale B S hS X.1⦄ (g : Z ⟶ Q), T.arrows g →
      (((smallBaseChangeModulePushforward B S hS f hf).obj F).val.map g.op) x ∈
        (Stacks.Sites.presheafIdealSmul (O := structureSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2) I
          (⊤ : ((smallBaseChangeModulePushforward B S hS f hf).obj F).Submodule).toSubmodule).obj
          (op Z)) :
    x ∈ (Stacks.Sites.idealSmul (O := structureSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2)
      (pullbackIdealSubsheaf B S hS f hf I) (⊤ : F.Submodule)).obj
        (op ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q)) := by
  refine Stacks.Sites.mem_idealSmul_of_mem (O := structureSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2) (M := F)
    (I := pullbackIdealSubsheaf B S hS f hf I) (N := (⊤ : F.Submodule))
    (T := Sieve.functorPushforward (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf) T)
    ((coverPreserving_smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).cover_preserve hT) ?_
  rintro W w ⟨Q', g, w', hg, rfl⟩
  have h2 := mem_presheafIdealSmul_pullback_of_mem_pushforward B S hS f hf I F Q' (hmem g hg)
  have h3 := (Stacks.Sites.presheafIdealSmul (O := structureSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2)
    (pullbackIdealSubsheaf B S hS f hf I) (⊤ : F.Submodule).toSubmodule).map_mem w'.op h2
  have key : F.val.map (w' ≫ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).map g).op x =
      F.val.map w'.op (F.val.map ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).map g).op x) :=
    PresheafOfModules.map_comp_apply F.val
      ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).map g).op w'.op x
  exact key ▸ h3

/-- **One inclusion of Stacks 0GF8**: for a representable morphism `f : Y ⟶ X` of algebraic
spaces, a sheaf of modules `F` on `Y` and a sheaf of ideals `I ⊆ 𝒪_X`,

`I · f_*F ⊆ f_*((f⁻¹I) · F)`

as subsheaves of `f_*F`, read on sections over every étale chart `Q` of `X`: the sections of
`f_*F` over `Q` are the sections of `F` over `Q ×_X Y`, and the inclusion is the one of the two
products of sections there.

Neither affineness of `f` nor quasi-coherence is used.  The opposite inclusion is the one that
needs them; see the implementation notes. -/
theorem mem_idealSmul_pullback_of_mem_pushforward (Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    {x : F.val.obj (op ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q))}
    (hx : x ∈ (Stacks.Sites.idealSmul (O := structureSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2) I
      (⊤ : ((smallBaseChangeModulePushforward B S hS f hf).obj F).Submodule)).obj (op Q)) :
    x ∈ (Stacks.Sites.idealSmul (O := structureSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2)
      (pullbackIdealSubsheaf B S hS f hf I) (⊤ : F.Submodule)).obj
        (op ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q)) := by
  have h :=
    (Stacks.Sites.mem_idealSmul_iff (O := structureSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2)
      (M := (smallBaseChangeModulePushforward B S hS f hf).obj F) (I := I)
      (N := (⊤ : ((smallBaseChangeModulePushforward B S hS f hf).obj F).Submodule))
      (Z := op Q) (x := x)).1 hx
  obtain ⟨T, hT, hmem⟩ := h
  exact mem_idealSmul_pullback_of_forall B S hS f hf I F Q hT hmem

end

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
